          <div class="stat"><b>∞</b><span>rebuild opportunities</span></div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <div class="callout">
        <strong>How to use this roadmap:</strong> Build → Rebuild → Improve →
        Combine. Do not treat every project as a disposable tutorial. Rebuild
        important projects with better architecture as you progress.
      </div>

      <section class="section" id="complete-curriculum">
        <div class="section-kicker">MASTER CURRICULUM</div>
        <h2>Complete Frontend → Backend Curriculum</h2>
        <p class="lead">
          A topic-by-topic checklist covering the areas that were missing: CSS
          depth, UI/UX, animation, accessibility, browser APIs, TypeScript,
          testing, architecture, backend engineering, databases, security,
          DevOps, system design and production.
        </p>

        <div class="curriculum-grid">
          <article class="topic-card" id="html-mastery">
            <h3>01 · HTML & Web Platform</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Document structure, doctype, head/body, semantic HTML</li>
              <li>Headings, sections, article, nav, main, aside, footer</li>
              <li>
                Links, images, picture/srcset, figure/figcaption, audio/video
              </li>
              <li>
                Forms, labels, inputs, validation, select, textarea, datalist
              </li>
              <li>Tables, captions, thead/tbody/tfoot, accessibility</li>
              <li>Metadata, Open Graph, canonical, favicon, robots</li>
              <li>HTML entities, iframe, embed, dialogs, details/summary</li>
              <li>Web components basics, custom elements, templates, slots</li>
              <li>Progressive enhancement and graceful degradation</li>
            </ul>
          </article>

          <article class="topic-card" id="css-mastery">
            <h3>02 · CSS — Complete Mastery</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Selectors, specificity, inheritance, cascade, layers</li>
              <li>Box model, margin, padding, border, outline</li>
              <li>
                Display, overflow, positioning, stacking contexts, z-index
              </li>
              <li>Flexbox: axes, alignment, wrapping, sizing, ordering</li>
              <li>Grid: tracks, areas, auto-fit/auto-fill, minmax</li>
              <li>Responsive design, media/container queries, breakpoints</li>
              <li>Units: px, %, rem, em, vw/vh, svh/lvh/dvh, ch</li>
              <li>Typography, font loading, variable fonts, line-height</li>
              <li>Colors, gradients, opacity, blend modes, filters</li>
              <li>CSS variables, theming, design tokens</li>
              <li>Transitions, transforms, keyframes, timing functions</li>
              <li>Clip-path, masks, shapes, pseudo-elements</li>
              <li>Logical properties and RTL/LTR layouts</li>
              <li>Modern CSS nesting, :is(), :where(), :has(), @supports</li>
              <li>Container queries and responsive components</li>
              <li>CSS architecture: BEM, utility, component CSS, layers</li>
              <li>Print CSS and media-specific styling</li>
              <li>CSS debugging and DevTools</li>
              <li>Performance: reducing layout/paint/composite work</li>
            </ul>
          </article>

          <article class="topic-card" id="uiux">
            <h3>03 · UI / UX Design</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>
                Design principles: hierarchy, balance, contrast, proximity,
                repetition
              </li>
              <li>Information architecture and user flows</li>
              <li>Wireframes, low/high fidelity prototypes</li>
              <li>Layout grids, spacing systems, 8-point systems</li>
              <li>Typography systems and type scale</li>
              <li>Color theory, semantic colors, contrast</li>
              <li>Design tokens and component variants</li>
              <li>Buttons, inputs, cards, navigation, menus, dialogs</li>
              <li>
                States: default, hover, focus, active, disabled, loading, error,
                success, empty
              </li>
